# A genuine local primitive for the zero base Fourier mode

The original smooth family has a real-smooth Haar mean. The proved
one-variable Cauchy--Green integral supplies a scalar primitive on a
smaller actual open neighborhood. Its literal torus-constant family is
jointly smooth, has the required actual base derivative, and has zero
real vertical derivative in every direction. No period map or extra
solvability hypothesis is needed.

This is a scalar analytic input. It makes no assertion of cohomological
local generation, local freeness, or a higher-direct-image comparison.
